Recently I bought an Audiophile USB and managed to get it to work using =
alsa. I tested countless different alsa releases in attempting to get =
the card to work, or work more fully. As far as I can tell the card will =
only work for playback alone using the usb-audio driver in alsa drivers =
version 0.9.0rc5. It works quite nicely in performing this simple tast =
alsa i must say, i'm getting latency times that make the windows drivers =
pale into insignificance! Pretty much every other release since 0.9.0rc5 =
through to the current 0.9.2 either "half works" (when it plays sound =
you get whitenoise/yummy digital nastiness) or doesn't seem to work at =
all aside from some clicks and pops when i scroll around an audio file =
in XMMS. I was wondering if the developers know what they've changed =
since 0.9.0rc5 to stop the usb-audio driver from working with this card =
and if they intend to re-implement support in future versions? I was =
also wondering if it is possible to get this card to capture and do midi =
in/out?

I'm not an alsa/linux expert, but i'd be happy to test and report =
results for early version drivers that seek to get this card working in =
a fuller manner.

Cheers,=20

Jonathan

